re to  get more children to school safely and  labor put forward constructive proposals  like using libraries and leisure centers  it was possible to do this if government  had have thrown more into it it's not  possible in all school settings at the  moment to bring all children back  because there aren't enough bathrooms to  teach those smaller groups of people and  that's why the government should have  been using this period of lockdown to  enable more children to return to school  safely the government now say that  should they cut the social distancing  regulations from 2 meters to 1 meter  then well if the scientists had advised  that this week then of course that would  make a difference but I believe even  with the social distancing mesh  that we've got in place now at two  meters more children could have been  brought back into a school setting if  the government had have made the effort  to use other buildings to bring in  temporary staff to put up temporary  buildings those are the sorts of  measures that should have been taken  over the last few months because you  know by September children would have  missed out on six months of Education  the schools have done their best to  ensure home schooling but we know that  many children haven't accessed that it  is imperative that the government but  the needs of children in the education  of children first they're now being  complacent about getting all children  back by September but again I would urge  the government to do the work now to  make that possible and also to ensure  that those children who have fallen  behind are given more support to be able  to catch up so we don't have a  generation who are left behind and  locked out of future opportunities  because of mistakes made during this  pandemic now you have a very economic  background so I'm interested to know  about your thoughts on the current  economic picture in the United Kingdom  with figures out this week showing that  UK debt is greater th